# Covers: `at sync (trace.enter?)` and `at sync (trace.leave?)` fire on tag
#         entry and exit, around the scope body.
# matrix-row: tag-scope-events
# Legacy: legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/tag/enter-leave.chk
#
# The legacy fixture wrote `at (trace.enter?)`, because the old runtime
# ran a tag-event subscriber synchronously at the scope boundary and had
# no other mode.  Here the two modes are spelled apart: a plain
# `at (e?)` body is a spawned strand and lands after the installing strand
# next yields, an `at sync (e?)` body runs inline.  Only the sync form can
# bracket the scope body, which is what this fixture is about, so that is
# the form it uses; reactive/tag_enter_leave_determinism.chk pins the
# same ordering with a string accumulator instead of echo.
#
# The legacy source also opened with `var trace = Tag.new() | {}`; the
# trailing brace-block expression is not in the v1.0 parser and was never
# load-bearing here.

var trace = Tag.new()
at sync (trace.enter?) echo("enter")
at sync (trace.leave?) echo("leave")
trace: echo("Say hi")
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] *** enter
[00000000] *** Say hi
[00000000] *** leave
[00000000] nil
